[{"id":"conv-predict-row","itemId":"conv-layer","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 11.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">conv_row</code>, with the weights 2, −1 and 3 and the bias −1, works along the row 25 (hexadecimal), one position a cycle. <code class=\"nobreak\">left</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">centre</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">right</code> are the taps of the position on <code class=\"nobreak\">p</code>; at the rising edge that ends the cycle, <code class=\"nobreak\">decision</code> takes that position's decision. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">decision</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>Each logit is −1 plus the weights of the taps that are 1, and each decision shows in the cycle after its position. Position 1's taps are 1, 0, 1: −1 + 2 + 3 = 4, so 1 in cycle 2. Position 2 has only <code class=\"nobreak\">centre</code>: −1 − 1 = −2, so 0. Positions 3 and 6 have only <code class=\"nobreak\">left</code> (1: decide 1), position 4 only <code class=\"nobreak\">right</code> (2: decide 1), position 5 only <code class=\"nobreak\">centre</code> (−2: 0), and position 7 none (−1: 0).</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"conv-easy","source":"hdl/level-11/conv_row/conv_row_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":9,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"conv_row_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"p[3:0]","path":"conv_row_tb.p","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[1,"0001"],[2,"0010"],[3,"0011"],[4,"0100"],[5,"0101"],[6,"0110"],[7,"0111"]]},{"label":"left","path":"conv_row_tb.dut.left","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]]},{"label":"centre","path":"conv_row_tb.dut.centre","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[2,"1"],[3,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"]]},{"label":"right","path":"conv_row_tb.dut.right","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[2,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"]]},{"label":"decision","path":"conv_row_tb.decision","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[2,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"],[8,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","1","0","1","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"decision","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"conv-fill-pad","itemId":"conv-layer","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 11.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">conv_row</code> reads its taps from <code class=\"nobreak\">padded</code>, ten bits: the row <code class=\"nobreak\">x</code> with a 0 at each end, so that a tap outside the row reads 0. Fill in <code class=\"nobreak\">padded</code>, so that the three lines under it pick position p's taps.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>{1'b0, x, 1'b0}</code>. A concatenation lists its parts from the top bit down (lesson 4.3), so <code class=\"nobreak\">padded[0]</code> is a 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">padded[1]</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">padded[8]</code> are <code class=\"nobreak\">x[0]</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">x[7]</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">padded[9]</code> is a 0. Then <code class=\"nobreak\">padded[p]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">x[p-1]</code>, and reads the 0 at position 0; <code>padded[p + 2]</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">x[p+1]</code>, and reads the other 0 at position 7.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-11/conv_row/conv_row.sv","firstLine":21,"totalLines":49,"before":["  logic [9:0]        padded;            // the row with a 0 each side","  logic              left, centre, right;","  logic signed [9:0] logit;",""],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign padded = ","right":";"},"after":["  assign left   = padded[p];            // x[p-1]","  assign centre = padded[p + 4'd1];     // x[p]","  assign right  = padded[p + 4'd2];     // x[p+1]"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground